        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): reject malformed ChatGPT timestamps",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves ChatGPT imports accepted malformed Unix timestamp strings like scientific notation or trailing newlines, which could normalize bad source data into valid page timestamps.  ## Why This Change Was Made Tightened isoFromUnix to only accept finite numeric values or canonical decimal strings, and added a CLI regression test covering malformed ChatGPT timestamp inputs.  ## User Impact ChatGPT imports now reject malformed timestamp text instead of silently accepting it. Valid imports are unchanged.  ## Evidence - Current head $head: focused Vitest on extensions/memory-wiki/src/cli.test.ts passed. - Current head $head: real CLI import proof passed for canonical valid timestamps, scientific-notation rejection, trailing-newline rejection, and signed fallback preservation.",
